# Held-out corpus text — prereg C11/C26.
#
# liu_2005, tang_2025 and wheaton_2004 are the only uncontaminated papers left in the motion
# corpus. Reading their text in any form destroys their value permanently, and a recursive
# search is enough to do it: on 2026-10-22 a repo-wide `grep` for "/C2" printed a verbatim
# wheaton_2004 methods sentence out of results/subject_corpus_sweep.txt, and a second search
# evaluated its pattern against held-out-named result JSONs. Neither opened a PDF; both show the
# hold-out was a reader's discipline rather than a property of the repository.
#
# SCOPE, STATED HONESTLY: ripgrep (rg) reads this file. PLAIN `grep -r` DOES NOT. Both incidents
# above came from `grep`, so this closes the rg path only. The remaining protection is the habit
# of excluding these ids explicitly, which is why they are also named in
# extractor_mvp/scripts/motion_probe.py (_HELD_OUT, refused before a client is built) and in
# scripts/glyph_leak_prediction.py (booleans-only output).

*liu_2005*
*tang_2025*
*wheaton_2004*

# Stores verbatim methods sentences for the whole corpus, held-out papers included.
extractor_mvp/results/subject_corpus_sweep.txt

# Listed although it is covered by *liu_2005* above, because it is the one held-out artifact that
# is deliberately TRACKED: it is a pipeline INPUT (scripts/run_pending_target_space.py:31 feeds it
# as liu_2005's methods slice). It stays in git and stays out of searches.
ground_truth/liu_2005_deinterleaved_methods.txt
